{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And they shall eat them.</b> Aaron and his sons — since they are their owners." "<b>With which atonement was made.</b> Any outsider [who eats] is an abomination." "<b>To fill their hands.</b> With this ram and this bread." "<b>To sanctify them.</b> For through these ordination offerings their hands were filled and they were sanctified for the priesthood." "<b>For holy they are.</b> Holy of holies; and from here we learn a warning to the outsider who eats holy of holies, for Scripture gave a reason for the matter — because holy they are (Leviticus 24)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {4 "Rashi's citation פסח' כ\"כ seemingly points to Leviticus 24 but the specific verse reference is uncertain; rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:37.875497760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}